WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.655
Now let's translate business rules into relational
decisions If every

00:00:05.681 --> 00:00:10.379
appointment belongs to exactly one patient
appointment needs a non-null patient foreign

00:00:10.392 --> 00:00:15.885
key A patient may exist before any appointment is
scheduled so the

00:00:15.911 --> 00:00:21.457
patient table does not require a child appointment
row The same reasoning

00:00:21.484 --> 00:00:27.012
applies to provider An appointment may have zero or
many service lines

00:00:27.301 --> 00:00:32.835
so those optional child rows belong in appointment
service A service can

00:00:32.861 --> 00:00:36.651
appear in many appointments which confirms that
appointment and service form a

00:00:36.677 --> 00:00:42.418
many-to-many relationship The key habit is to read
the business sentence first

00:00:42.681 --> 00:00:46.023
then decide where the foreign key belongs and
whether that relationship is

00:00:46.049 --> 00:00:47.299
required or optional
